{title: At the Cross}
{artist: Isaac Watts & Ralph Hudson}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
A[Eb]las! and did my [Ab]Savior [Eb]bleed, and did my Sovereign [Bb]die?
Would [Eb]he devote that [Ab]sacred [Eb]head for [Bb]sinners such as [Eb]I?

Chorus
At the cross, at the cross, where I [Ab]first saw the light,
and the [Eb]burden of my heart rolled a[Bb]way —
it was [Eb]there by faith [Ab]I received my [Eb]sight,
and [Cm]now I [Bb]am happy [Eb]all the day!
